A product capture now reserves one analysis, guides the user to its supplier shop, downloads cleaned shop HTML, then captures the factory profile or finishes with product/shop evidence. Visible supplier headers are accepted when the company-introduction module is absent; the extractor marks this as header-only evidence. Users may dismiss CAPTCHA overlays themselves when underlying content is visible.

This release includes the collection API and migration 0017, durable owner-scoped capture/replay, bounded sanitized HTML enrichment, queued saved-upload assessment/reporting, review drawer retention, source provenance and insufficient-evidence scoring fixes. It also adds a separate live-origin extension build without replacing the localhost artifact. No secrets, raw operator webpages or uncommitted planning changes are included.

Validation: 1,085 backend tests passed (32 environment skips) against PostgreSQL; 158 frontend tests and TypeScript passed. Local browser fixture checks cover product/shop/factory capture and header-only evidence. The operator confirmed the live-page header capture works. The reported local failed analysis was retried after network recovery under its original ID and completed with persisted assessment/report, without another quota slot. Production web and live-origin extension builds and the frontend credential scan passed. GitHub image/browser checks and deployed end-to-end verification gate publication.
